# Registry blocks — Tailwind-first styling

This project uses **Tailwind CSS v4** via `app/globals.css` (`@import "tailwindcss"`, `@theme inline`). Blocks do not ship their own Tailwind entry.

## Default: utilities on TSX

Put layout, typography, spacing, and colors on `className` in `.tsx`:

```tsx
<h2 className="text-4xl font-medium leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.03em] lg:text-5xl">
  Title{" "}
  <span className="font-serif italic font-normal tracking-[-0.01em]">accent</span>
</h2>
<p className="max-w-xl text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground" />
```

Use theme utilities: `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-background`, `border-border`, `font-mono`, `font-serif`, `rounded-lg`, etc.

Do **not** add block-prefixed classes for simple one-off typography (e.g. `.fsv5-heading { font-weight: 500; }`).

Do **not** use `hsl(var(--foreground))` in CSS — use `var(--foreground)` or Tailwind tokens (`:root` is oklch).

## When block `.css` is allowed

Keep a sibling `*.css` import only for what utilities cannot express cleanly:

- `@keyframes` and `animation`
- `::before` / `::after` (rules, bullets, device chrome)
- Complex grids with `nth-child` placement (bento, brand grids)
- Marquee tracks and infinite scroll
- GSAP / scroll hooks (`[data-*]`, opacity shells)
- Mock-UI **scoped variables** (`--gc-*`, `--cb-*`, `--ss-*`, `--crt-t-*`, `--pp-*`, …) for authentic app chrome colors
- Descendant overrides (e.g. `.hero-v8 .scb-root { font-family: inherit }`)

Trim each rule block as you migrate; delete the CSS file if nothing remains.

## Do not

- Add `tailwind.config.js` or `@import "tailwindcss"` inside a block folder
- Use `@apply` in block CSS for new work (prefer TSX utilities)
- Create `components/`, `hooks/`, `lib/`, or `styles/` subfolders under a block (flat layout per `registry-blocks-source-layout.mdc`)

## After edits

Run `pnpm registry:build` and declare every file in `registry.json`.
